# ============================================================================
# setup/link.conf.local.example
#
# Optional host-specific override overlay.
# Copy to setup/link.conf.local (which is gitignored) ONLY if you need to
# override default settings from link.conf on this specific machine.
#
# Production defaults are already set in link.conf:
#   POWER_SOURCE=external   (full field power)
#   WIFI_TXPOWER=1500       (15 dBm)
#   QGC_HOST=listen         (GS listens on 0.0.0.0:14550 for QGC connections)
#
# Uncomment and adjust below only what you want to override.
#
# After editing:
#   sudo ./install.sh --role air|gs --only 50-config
#   sudo systemctl restart wifibroadcast@drone   # or wifibroadcast@gs
# ============================================================================

# --- Bench work / Low-power testing (either host) ----------------------------
# Use this when powering the radio module directly from the Raspberry Pi USB port
# without external power / BEC. Caps power to avoid brownouts.
# POWER_SOURCE=usb-pi
# WIFI_TXPOWER=500

# --- MAVLink custom routing (GS only) ----------------------------------------
# By default, GS listens on 0.0.0.0:14550 (QGC_HOST=listen).
# If you want GS to push UDP telemetry directly to a fixed laptop IP instead:
# QGC_HOST=192.168.1.50
# Or for QGC running locally on the Pi itself:
# QGC_HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- Air unit custom serial port (Air only) ----------------------------------
# If your flight controller telemetry is on a USB-serial adapter instead of UART:
# MAVLINK_SERIAL=/dev/ttyUSB0


